{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters","id":1102537,"title":"[2E] Archeomancy for Masters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-06-11T09:35:34-07:00","id":1102537,"title":"[2E] Archeomancy for Masters","content":"I run three years long chronicle with Masters and Double Adepts PCs. After last game session, I was told by players to stop making combat scenes because they are too short living ( with less powerful enemies ) or only too long taking ( if monster have a lot Resistant trait, Size or some Unbreakable or like this Numina ), but repeating in spellcasting. As we have Archeomancy lead game, players wants more puzzles. <b>But <i>how</i> can I make puzzles or any Archeomancy-like challenges for them if they literally can make things out of thin air?</b><br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> 'PC1: We need lead key to open those doors. - PC2: No sweat, I have Master of Matter, I just conjure it.'<br /> 'PC1: We need to get to Katmandu to get Rod of Seroth. - PC2: I just open portal to other part of world.'<br /> <br /> <b><i>Anything</i> that were putted against protagonists in Indiana Jones movies or Tomb Raider games is futile, from my POV, any real challenge.</b> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I could simple go on next game session '<i>And you got to last three Chakras, talked to Archmasters, and solved world problems - The End of chronicle</i>'. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> On this last session we had Astral journey and players were starting it on the Synesi to Omphalos Realm - they spend an hour of real world time on session to get to the way of opening Omphalos Stone to get to the way, becoming more and more irritated, by each failed attempt. ( That anyone of them did not thought about remembering hints from Orders training on Astral is beyond my own recognition, here. )<br /> <br /> If each puzzle I make must be 'And you need to tune melody of 9th Symphony of Beethoven', all game will be just puzzle mess. Mess PC <i>still </i>will solve in seconds, even the players will be irritated by trying all things by hours in real world time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-11-2017, 12:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T09:45:06-07:00","id":1102541,"title":"","content":"That's why you don't let your players reach mastery. You conclude their story by that point. How to make things harder? Not any type of lead would work. Get the portal opener cursed so he can't just teleport them.<br /> <br /> It's start to get unfair, since they can't use the abilities that by all means they've earned already. Or maybe, dunno, have them take apprentices and deal with their bullshit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12191,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","user":"Malus","date":". 06-11-2017, 12:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T10:26:32-07:00","id":1102554,"title":"","content":"Adamas, adamas, adamas... Potents ward and ban. And many more.<br /> Check Secrets of the Ruined Temple. A lot of things are still relevant in 2nd edition, especially concerning this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T12:21:12-07:00","id":1102575,"title":"","content":"Well. Put some arch-level antimagic barrier on parts of the complex and let them struggle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T13:37:47-07:00","id":1102599,"title":"","content":"If they are only 1st degree Masters, that means they aren't Masters in at least 5 or so Arcana, right (assuming 5 players, each of a different Path)?<br /> <br /> Look at the spells listed and look for what they <i>can't</i> do, or require excessive Reach to do so. Then throw those problems at them. They get notified of an event that has passed beyond their ability to time-travel back to, or encounter conditions that require impossible or exotic materials <i>as a starting point</i>. Remember Spell Control - they can only have so many spells active at once before Paradox starts creeping in. Overload their abilities to just answer everything with magic. Have opponents with access to counterspelling powers, or ruins that trigger traps when magic is used nearby.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T14:07:17-07:00","id":1102606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102599#post1102599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are only 1st degree Masters, that means they aren't Masters in at least 5 or so Arcana, right (assuming 5 players, each of a different Path)?<br /> <br /> Look at the spells listed and look for what they <i>can't</i> do, or require excessive Reach to do so. Then throw those problems at them. They get notified of an event that has passed beyond their ability to time-travel back to, or encounter conditions that require impossible or exotic materials <i>as a starting point</i>. Remember Spell Control - they can only have so many spells active at once before Paradox starts creeping in. Overload their abilities to just answer everything with magic. Have opponents with access to counterspelling powers, or ruins that trigger traps when magic is used nearby.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure they're second degree masters, if I remember wyrd's various posts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T14:34:54-07:00","id":1102613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102606#post1102606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure they're second degree masters, if I remember wyrd's various posts.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Meh. My points still stand, the job just becomes harder. Even Masters have limits to what they can accomplish.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T15:03:32-07:00","id":1102618,"title":"","content":"A friend who has been STing the same Mage game for the last 3 years has player characters with similar power levels. Being able to do high level magic doesn't mean you can automatically solve all your problems with it unless you as the ST allow it.<br /> <br /> Also, you should be doing what not only makes the most narrative sense, but what has the better narrative flow. If they're stumped on a puzzle, then set things up to move the game forward without them solving it, or so that they have to abandon the puzzle temporarily so you can drop a hint and say to them, &quot;It occurs to you this could help with that puzzle you were struggling with earlier.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sometimes players and their characters fail, don't be afraid to fail them. Plan out what happens in the event of a success or a failure instead of hinging everything on their success. This can lead to interesting directions for the story, and may wrap around to later success. <br /> <br /> Seriously, none of your problems stem from the mechanics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T16:54:47-07:00","id":1102650,"title":"","content":"Without knowing the particulars of what you're trying to do-seriously, ancient ruins have a <i>purpose, </i>and must be built in accordance to that purpose-four particulars come to mind.<br /> <br /> A) Know the limits of what your characters can do.<br /> B) Build your sites likes like you do explosive ordinance-a series of systems that when improperly handled collapse the whole, or perhaps significant chunks, of the site. Make it clear to the players that this is the case as part of the buy-in.<br /> C) Think like a locksmith in regards to your mechanical mysteries-your keys* are particular, not generic. Not just anything will do, it has to be the <i>just</i> right thing.<br /> D) As always, flow with the characters. You do want to challenge them, and the game gives you particulars for making that happen. Masters(First, Second, Third, whatever) are <i>not</i> gods, and you can always find a limit to their powers-that said, you don't want to block them either. Feel things out and work with what's on the paper.<br /> <br /> I feel the same can probably said from your comments on combat, though again I can't comment without particular examples-but an easy answer is always to come at them sideways rather than up front. Rather then emphasizing Resistances and such, create combat scenarios with <i>conseqeunces</i>, particularly ones where the priorities need juggling, and a mis-handling of them will, again, collapse the entire thing around the PC's ears.<br /> <br /> * Obviously I'm not talking about literal keys all the time, rather I am speaking of &quot;solutions to the problems&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T16:58:22-07:00","id":1102651,"title":"","content":"Also consider that if you're having problems with coming up with challenges and conseqeunces for them, maybe it's time to admit you're at your limits, give them a conclusion, and move onto something else.<br /> <br /> What I would actually encourage you to do, though, is give us some examples of what you're actually doing(or even better yet, planning on doing), and see if we can brainstorm better ways to approach the matter and lay out a groundwork of how to approach things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T23:23:33-07:00","id":1102714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102554#post1102554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Adamas, adamas, adamas... Potents ward and ban. And many more.<br /> Check Secrets of the Ruined Temple. A lot of things are still relevant in 2nd edition, especially concerning this topic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re-reading now <b>Secrets of The Ruined Temple</b>...<br /> <br /> <b>Adamas in 1E was Reducing Successes, based on power of this process ( 1, 3 and 6 Successes versions ).<br /> <br /> So I assume in 2E Adamas will work as Withstood of item/place? Or BONUS to starting Withstood based on Durability of original material?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-12-2017, 04:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T23:25:50-07:00","id":1102715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102575#post1102575\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well. Put some arch-level antimagic barrier on parts of the complex and let them struggle.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>How</i> can anyone pass Archmastery barriers? They are 'automatic standing up' spells ( by Practice of Dynamics, I suppose ) - you kill it, next turn it's once again in process.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-11T23:32:33-07:00","id":1102717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102599#post1102599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are only 1st degree Masters, that means they aren't Masters in at least 5 or so Arcana, right (assuming 5 players, each of a different Path)?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102606#post1102606\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure they're second degree masters, if I remember wyrd's various posts.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have six players, of all Paths beside Thyrsus. All of them are 1st Degree Masters ( Mastery in only one Arcanum ) or 2nd Degree Adepts ( Adepts in two Arcana ).<br /> <br /> Or, in simpler terms, highest Arcana ratings in cabal from my memory - Death 5, Fate 4, Forces 4, Life 3, Matter 5, Mind 4, Prime 4, Spirit 4, Space 4, Time 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-12-2017, 04:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T01:15:38-07:00","id":1102728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102618#post1102618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you should be doing what not only makes the most narrative sense, but what has the better narrative flow. If they're stumped on a puzzle, then set things up to move the game forward without them solving it, or so that they have to abandon the puzzle temporarily so you can drop a hint and say to them, &quot;It occurs to you this could help with that puzzle you were struggling with earlier.&quot;<br /> <br /> Sometimes players and their characters fail, don't be afraid to fail them. Plan out what happens in the event of a success or a failure instead of hinging everything on their success. This can lead to interesting directions for the story, and may wrap around to later success.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great, but sometimes there SHOULD be only one entrance - other way you would have particular Temple of Times Before uncovered millenia ago. In this particular instance, it's Anima Mundi domain on Whorl ( Chantry of pre-Fall (?) Archmaster's ). Finding entrance on 'Astral Path' to it ( from Omphalos realm to Whorl, after 'silver footprints' of Archmaster ) <i>is </i>a test made by Archmaster. I.E. Logical in narrative logic ( and relative easy if anyone of them thought about asking something like 'what they teach me about Astral and Big Stone in Order trening' ).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102618#post1102618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seriously, none of your problems stem from the mechanics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, but I still ask for advises how to run Archeomancy on this level in this topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T01:45:58-07:00","id":1102735,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\">So I've played in and run a couple of Mastery chronicles. I will say that I don't know how to force the kind of puzzles that you're looking for. I don't know if it's possible when you're dealing with people that are so powerful. However...<br /> <br /> In every single one of our games that progressed that far, the Masters created enough of their own problems to worry about.<br /> Needing a lead key? Needing to travel halfway around the world? Those aren't challenges, those are roadblocks, and of course Masters can dispense with them with ease.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">&quot;The multitude of Rank 5 Spirits I've bound into my flesh are waking up and starting to influence the world around me, but I can't release them without causing an even bigger problem&quot; is a Master problem.<br /> &quot;I've accidentally created a Timeline where everything I love and cherish is gone&quot; is a Master problem<br /> &quot;I pissed off an Exarch and spent seven years outside of time hiding from them&quot; is a Master problem</span><br /> <br /> If your players are Masters and they are unambitious enough to not be attempting anything that ever causes problems for themselves, there's probably not a lot left for you in the Chronicle. Forcing external story at this level isn't likely to work well.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T01:52:38-07:00","id":1102736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102650#post1102650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Without knowing the particulars of what you're trying to do-seriously, ancient ruins have a <i>purpose, </i>and must be built in accordance to that purpose-four particulars come to mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>This particular site in my mind is Anima Mundi domain where preOrders Archmaster made his Chantry and is built to test possible Hieromagus candidates. Archmaster is from Vajrastra Darshana - he even describe as ( and believes ) he is Hindu god Chandramas ( 'Moon'). What does it says about sight beyond he would rather want to Duel with possible candidates, and maybe make some arena chamber in his place?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102650#post1102650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A) Know the limits of what your characters can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found that, in practice, there is very little in 2E Adept mages <i>cannot make instantly</i> if we talk about places that are not like deep space vacuum. Whenever is <i>some</i> of their Adept Arcanum Pattern, things are solevable by them. Masters just makes it much simpler by Making or Unmaking Practices.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102650#post1102650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">B) Build your sites likes like you do explosive ordinance-a series of systems that when improperly handled collapse the whole, or perhaps significant chunks, of the site. Make it clear to the players that this is the case as part of the buy-in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Great general advise for Temples sites \u2013 only my own chronicle is based on idea that most of those Archmasters <i>live</i> there. I was having one site with Death mage that worked as mummy already \u2013 and I have in mind one place where Archamsters is already gone ( well, moved in Time Stream, so to speak ). Other than that, all Temples I run are also Chantries of Archmasters \u2013 they would <i>not</i> want places that will destroy by wrong answer/move of PCs. MAYBE I can mark that if they diverge from path, they will not find \u2018heart of Temple\u2019 ( i.e. proper Chantry )?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102650#post1102650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">C) Think like a locksmith in regards to your mechanical mysteries-your keys* are particular, not generic. Not just anything will do, it has to be the <i>just</i> right thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>So PCs should go on and off to the Temple site to bring the Keys they did not know about before? Like this probable scene\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2018PC1: We stand before Main Gate. How to get inside? \u2013 PC2: There is inscription in High Speech. It says something about Rod of Sorapth. \u2013 PC3: What is this thing? And hell, how do we may know where to find it?!\u2019<br /> <br /> <b>Still, my cabal have Space Adept, so teleportation is possible in their way. Breaking scene with stealing some old relic from museum or private collection is interesting, I must say. </b><b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102650#post1102650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">D) As always, flow with the characters. You do want to challenge them, and the game gives you particulars for making that happen. Masters(First, Second, Third, whatever) are <i>not</i> gods, and you can always find a limit to their powers-that said, you don't want to block them either. Feel things out and work with what's on the paper.<br /> <br /> I feel the same can probably said from your comments on combat, though again I can't comment without particular examples-but an easy answer is always to come at them sideways rather than up front. Rather then emphasizing Resistances and such, create combat scenarios with <i>conseqeunces</i>, particularly ones where the priorities need juggling, and a mis-handling of them will, again, collapse the entire thing around the PC's ears.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like mentioned before \u2013 After running 2E on year now, I found very difficult to challenge Adept level PCs. They can get anything they want, if they need it. Making consequences with site is maybe good advice \u2013 but hard pressed in place that is also Archmasters home. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-12-2017, 05:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T01:57:33-07:00","id":1102737,"title":"","content":"Side note: I plan to make Time Travel story, but it's in other place PC will come - probably as next on the list. For now, I run Astral Temple/Chantry idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T02:15:21-07:00","id":1102740,"title":"","content":"Well, one thing about Archmasters - they are usually a lot more resilient than their lessers. If a building drops on them, so what? They've rendered themselves impervious the physical assault, and they can rebuild the temple or rewind time once the I have been dealt with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T02:33:16-07:00","id":1102744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102714#post1102714\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Re-reading now <b>Secrets of The Ruined Temple</b>...<br /> <br /> <b>Adamas in 1E was Reducing Successes, based on power of this process ( 1, 3 and 6 Successes versions ).<br /> <br /> So I assume in 2E Adamas will work as Withstood of item/place? Or BONUS to starting Withstood based on Durability of original material?</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> M:tAw2 p244, Adamas cannot be affected by Matter spells. Period. This provide unpenetrable barrier that force the players to work within the constraints of the Ruin, answering its enigmas and fighting its guardians, rather than bypassing its protections.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3648-nepher","name":"Nepher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3648_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T03:24:22-07:00","id":1102749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nepher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102744#post1102744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">M:tAw2 p244, Adamas cannot be affected by Matter spells. Period. This provide unpenetrable barrier that force the players to work within the constraints of the Ruin, answering its enigmas and fighting its guardians, rather than bypassing its protections.</div> </div> </div> </div>So yes, Adamas EVERYWHERE will be in my Temples from now on! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> But there are some questions to Adamas I have. For ease of discussion, I will share with you on image of place I run with now ( and players have this as 'session invitation' - i.e Facebook event ). Let's assume I have this kind of palace and it's walls, made wholly from Adamas:<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/ir0DIkJ.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Here are ways I could get inside if only buildings are made Adamas - answer me how to stop it. Still, it's just outer walls - maybe let players use those 'shortcuts'? They will still have problems in changing buildings <i>inside</i> the Palace made of Adamas.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>Matter mage cannot change walls and buildings. BUT he<i> can </i>transform and shape ground or air around them</b>. He just makes <b>Full Metal Alchemist</b>-like pillars that will go over the walls. Ground around buildings is<b> not </b>made of Adamas, obviously.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><br /> <img src=\"https://vignette2.wikia.nocookie.net/fairytail/images/d/d9/Jura_attacks_Jellal.png/revision/latest?cb=20121208054855\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> 2. <b>Spirit mage can just walk to walls, go over to Shadow Realm and awaken the Spirit of the Palace walls. </b>Walls Spirit then can directly shape walls, even if made of Adamas - spirit's powers are <i>not</i> Matter Arcanum, are not even spells per se - they are just supernatural abilities of 'god' of walls around Palace. Adamas is not 'antimagic material' - it's just superdurable version of original material.<br /> <br /> And that's only two simple solutions I got on top of my head. Some ideas you got on those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-12-2017, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T03:32:58-07:00","id":1102752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102728#post1102728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Great, but sometimes there SHOULD be only one entrance - other way you would have particular Temple of Times Before uncovered millenia ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>You should reread my post, I didn't say have more than one entrance. I'm talking about how to handle narrative flow so that you aren't wasting hours of your player's time on making them solve a puzzle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T03:50:24-07:00","id":1102755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102749#post1102749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. [B]Spirit mage can just walk to walls, go over to Shadow Realm and awaken the Spirit of the Palace walls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have them already awake? A Spirit with Influence: Chantry 5 or something like that.<br /> <br /> That said, why does the chantry need to test them via a puzzle. I mean, I get you're trying to copy Indiana Jones or Tomb Raider, but... what does a logic puzzle have to do with being the Hieromagus?<br /> <br /> I mean, surely the fact they found the chantry is the puzzle. The Arc of the Covenant was just in a big vault, the puzzle was tracking it down. (Yeah, I know Last Crusade has puzzles but it didn't make much sense there either.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T03:58:57-07:00","id":1102756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102715#post1102715\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <i>How</i> can anyone pass Archmastery barriers? They are 'automatic standing up' spells ( by Practice of Dynamics, I suppose ) - you kill it, next turn it's once again in process.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Let them use mundane drills and shoot some monster without magic. Get them out of their comfort zone for an hour.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T04:16:59-07:00","id":1102757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102756#post1102756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Let them use mundane drills and shoot some monster without magic. Get them out of their comfort zone for an hour.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good idea on Material Realm Temples. But how to make them drill under in Astral, as they can simply 'dream things up'?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T04:22:48-07:00","id":1102758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102736#post1102736\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like mentioned before \u2013 After running 2E on year now, I found very difficult to challenge Adept level PCs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Re: Combat Encounters<br /> Should the same not be true for any *NPC* with Arcana at 4+? I'm not just talking about Mages - Supernal Beings qualify, too. <br /> <br /> Unless you're intentionally handicapping what their adversaries can do, there should be absolutely zero chance that combat at this level isn't incredibly dangerous and nerve-wracking for all involved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T04:28:46-07:00","id":1102760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102755#post1102755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have them already awake? A Spirit with Influence: Chantry 5 or something like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>On Spirit 4 Arcanum is simple matter of 3-4 spells, you know... And Influence: Chantry 4 would be needed only to reshape walls in to new gate, i.e. change the thing under Influence.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102755#post1102755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, why does the chantry need to test them via a puzzle. I mean, I get you're trying to copy Indiana Jones or Tomb Raider, but... what does a logic puzzle have to do with being the Hieromagus?</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if we concentrate on my Hieromagus plotline - <b>HOW to test someone for Messiah of Magic? Beside testing their Wisdom?</b><br /> <br /> And this topic is general one -<b> I also question for ideas how to run puzzles for Masters characters - as <i>explicit</i> I was ask from players on that.</b><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102755#post1102755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, surely the fact they found the chantry is the puzzle. The Arc of the Covenant was just in a big vault, the puzzle was tracking it down. (Yeah, I know Last Crusade has puzzles but it didn't make much sense there either.)</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Secrets of the Ruined Temple</b> points that puzzles and tests are part of any Temple. Mages of Time Before were sadists. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-12-2017, 07:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T04:56:13-07:00","id":1102763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102749#post1102749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. <b>Spirit mage can just walk to walls, go over to Shadow Realm and awaken the Spirit of the Palace walls. </b>Walls Spirit then can directly shape walls, even if made of Adamas - spirit's powers are <i>not</i> Matter Arcanum, are not even spells per se - they are just supernatural abilities of 'god' of walls around Palace. Adamas is not 'antimagic material' - it's just superdurable version of original material.</div> </div> </div> </div>So... well, i'd say they could go and awaken the Spirit Temple (if that's even possible, as the temple could be the Archmaster Golden Road Itself, so there's no real temple to awaken, it would be in fact the Archmage soul), but <b>NOT</b> a wall of it, dammit :'D <br /> <br /> If they are so... &quot;bold&quot; (the pronunciation goes much more close to foolish) to awaken the Spirit of an Archmage temple, why on Earth they should be able to control it? Not only because they have no Thyrsus, but also because of the sheer power of the building. Even in the case that <b><i>you</i></b> feel <b><i>compelled to let them</i></b> control it... how about the logic of it? They command them to surrender the sanctum of itself and the building, operating on its own logic, guides them to a merry chase in the spiritual world, eventually leading to a Shadow reflection of the building, to the spirit core. Just a quick example.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T05:13:35-07:00","id":1102765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102757#post1102757\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Good idea on Material Realm Temples. But how to make them drill under in Astral, as they can simply 'dream things up'?</div> </div> </div> </div>Can they? I'm not sure how mechanics of 'dreaming up' work when you're outside of you oneiros, cause it has been a long time since I read Astral Realms but if you accept archmastery spell that forbids magic, blocking 'dreaming up' looks like a childs play for an archmaster.<br /> Even if they can do it I doubt that they can dream 'magic' without magic. They still have to drill and shoot enemies with tools available in the dream.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T05:20:19-07:00","id":1102771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102760#post1102760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On Spirit 4 Arcanum is simple matter of 3-4 spells, you know... And Influence: Chantry 4 would be needed only to reshape walls in to new gate, i.e. change the thing under Influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point is you could have the spirit already be awake and under the control of the Archmaster.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T05:21:32-07:00","id":1102772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102763#post1102763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If they are so... &quot;bold&quot; (the pronunciation goes much more close to foolish) to awaken the Spirit of an Archmage temple, why on Earth they should be able to control it? Not only because they have no Thyrsus, but also because of the sheer power of the building. Even in the case that <b><i>you</i></b> feel <b><i>compelled to let them</i></b> control it... how about the logic of it? They command them to surrender the sanctum of itself and the building, operating on its own logic, guides them to a merry chase in the spiritual world, eventually leading to a Shadow reflection of the building, to the spirit core. Just a quick example.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could you refrain this example in simpler English? I think you mean here to not make this whole thing only 3 spells for players, but I'm not sure and later description just miss my understanding of grammar and vocabulary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-12T05:27:00-07:00","id":1102773,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102771#post1102771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point is you could have the spirit already be awake and under the control of the Archmaster.</div> </div> </div> </div>If Archamster sounds as previous Spirit Mage in the first place. Giving every possible Arcana level to Archamasters seems to me as setting cheating. It's like 'I have general idea that this would be like Gnosis 7 Archmaster, with 2-3 Arcana past 6+ dots' - and then each one of them becomes god-like being with five Arcana past 6+ dots, only to block all PCs in cabal - that sounds... wrong to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T02:23:03-07:00","id":1103047,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102772#post1102772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could you refrain this example in simpler English? I think you mean here to not make this whole thing only 3 spells for players, but I'm not sure and later description just miss my understanding of grammar and vocabulary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually yes, and sorry! My english is getting worse by the day, i swear. What i meant with that last paragraph was: play with the alien nature of a Spirit Temple. Maybe the spirit cannot think in human therms. Maybe when they ask it to let them travel to its core -the Inner Sanctum so to speak- the only way it can help the players is providing them with a spiritual test, making them travel into the Shadow as a way of enlightment.<br /> <br /> I mean, this is the Spirit of an Archmage temple: at its core is the feeling of trascendence. Maybe it really cannot help anyone to travel trough its corridors; maybe is the travelers who need to unravel themselves and in doing so reaching the Inner Sanctum by themselves. <br /> <br /> In other words: don't make the progression about spells. Make the progression about Wisdom. Hope that helps!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T05:27:36-07:00","id":1103088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1102773#post1102773\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If Archamster sounds as previous Spirit Mage in the first place. Giving every possible Arcana level to Archamasters seems to me as setting cheating. It's like 'I have general idea that this would be like Gnosis 7 Archmaster, with 2-3 Arcana past 6+ dots' - and then each one of them becomes god-like being with five Arcana past 6+ dots, only to block all PCs in cabal - that sounds... wrong to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>It should. They're fallen beings trying to deal with the ascended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T05:47:52-07:00","id":1103095,"title":"","content":"They're NPCs, unless the players can cast spells on them to divine their stats then the stats can be whatever you need until the players figure their stats out.<br /> <br /> This is a big part of your problem <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> you keep writing yourself into a corner.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T08:38:51-07:00","id":1103150,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1103095#post1103095\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're NPCs, unless the players can cast spells on them to divine their stats then the stats can be whatever you need until the players figure their stats out.<br /> This is a big part of your problem <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1437_5.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1437\" data-vbnamecard=\"1437\">wyrdhamster</a> you keep writing yourself into a corner.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm with W<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">yrdhamster in that, though. I like to have my NPCs stated and fully (moooore or less) fleshed. If i'm pressed, i could make some changes before the PCs divine their strengths and weaknesses, but i don't like it. It's easy to come with an explanation about why that NPC could do that thing he is not supposed to, yes, but that's the easy way (unless said deviation has been thought as intentional, in which case is all part of the plot of course!). </span></span></span><br /> <br /> Anyway, there are plenty of solutions to these problems, and most of them start -or end- involving other Mages in those scenes too: as much as your PCs can do, other Master-degree NPCs exist, and their interests could be antagonistic. Things get suddenly much more difficult when that Temple you are searching has had its Spirit awakened by an enemy Thyrsus (i.e.) for her own reasons that could or could not have something to do with the players goals. That super-special leaden key? Seer's propriety. That sigil they have to forge? Requires the heart and soul of someone you love sacrificed in name of Anpu, and a ritual in whose casting the PC has to be helped by her sworn enemy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Userhat Aegpts Vlrs. </span><span style=\"color:#996633\">Coren &quot;Ojos de Fuego&quot;. </span><span style=\"color:#666699\">Mithrael. </span><span style=\"color:#ffcc00\">Menehet.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1349-phersus","name":"Phersus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1349_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T09:33:07-07:00","id":1103168,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Phersus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1102537-2e-archeomancy-for-masters?p=1103150#post1103150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, there are plenty of solutions to these problems, and most of them start -or end- involving other Mages in those scenes too: as much as your PCs can do, other Master-degree NPCs exist, and their interests could be antagonistic. Things get suddenly much more difficult when that Temple you are searching has had its Spirit awakened by an enemy Thyrsus (i.e.) for her own reasons that could or could not have something to do with the players goals. That super-special leaden key? Seer's propriety. That sigil they have to forge? Requires the heart and soul of someone you love sacrificed in name of Anpu, and a ritual in whose casting the PC has to be helped by her sworn enemy.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm more or less pass of introducing new forces in chronicle - we are going more for ending than starting the game. Still, I <i>was </i>thinking about uncovering Seer's mastermind behind hunters two interventions before they get in game, from two various hunter orgs, that I imagined good two years ago. Mastermind Seer in nothing short but Cardinal for the Minister of Paternostern ( on Christanity ) - Pontifex Maximus - that want's to assure his position of next Minister by killing Hieromagus reincarnation ( half of PCs cabal ). Was envisioning of scene showing him as very much mix of <b>Assassin's Creed Brotherhood </b>and <b>Young Pope</b> - but I clearly can send enemy pylon working for him, send to end their lives or close Temple before PCs will explore it. Having Spirit Seer working for Paternostern is not so big a sterach here then. <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </span></span></span>Still, some points from you on other parts of archeomancy/assassins pylon would be nice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=zzNs4-kRLaE\" data-code=\"zzNs4-kRLaE\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/zzNs4-kRLaE/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 06-13-2017, 04:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-13T13:22:58-07:00","id":1103249,"title":"","content":"So I was thinking about Obsessions and had this realization. Obsessions are the Mages' drugs, their higher Gnosis is an indicator of their increasing tolerance for it and thus their need for more of it, and it's not an indicator of their ability to actually handle more mysteries (Theoretically they can, but that's what drug addicts figure too). When dealing with high powered characters you should be setting it up so they bite off more than they can chew. Essentially, you should be building up to an OD on mysteries.<br /> <br /> Incidentally this fact that they're trying to take as much of their drugs as possible should be what you're using to counter the fact that at higher levels a focused Mage can handle almost anything. Overload them with choice and consequence and they won't be able to focus as effectively on solving a problem because they will actually be juggling several.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2632,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","user":"Mrmdubois","date":". 06-13-2017, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}